      "closure_rationale": "The original total clamped counter permits observation of a violated predicate without invalid C execution. The new byte primitive has a real index precondition: OFF disables reporting but cannot authorize an unsafe address. Actual enabled/disabled assert(++essential) executables observe1/0 on both compilers; essential effects cannot depend on assert. N1570 draft diagnostics and mutex passages are inspected, distinct from published C17/C23 access gaps. The bounded byte adapter rejects out-of-view indices in every mode, admits NULL only for an empty span, preserves bytes on refusal and preflights report exhaustion. Valid writes remain possible at reportMAX. Shared counter and byte paths use one actual mutex and the same report owner; snapshot stages under lock. Lock admission failure has no effect, unexpected unlock failure is explicitly fatal because state may have committed, and initialization/destruction require fresh or joined quiescent ownership. Six C11 compiler profiles execute5anchors,7compiled controls and5compiling-stub rejections. The independent integer/byte model checks182709ordinary counter cases plus invalid boundaries for182869total, and1188byte cases/profile. Actual ER_MUTANT15/16 and five new defects reject normally. The original harmless control changes byte5 outside an advertised3byte view inside an actual8byte object; no out-of-object execution or code-execution claim. All13cost dimensions and actual include/object/runtime evidence are retained. Delayed support runs four actual workers with1000byte and1000counter attempts each, producing exactly8000shared reports and a joined snapshot, then tests last-report exhaustion across both operations. Default C11 threads and an explicit POSIX backend retain separate APIs and lifetimes. GCC/Clang POSIX release/TSan runs pass; C11 TSan fails in the runtime and separate original minimal protected-write controls reproduce it, so no clean C11 TSan result is claimed. This supports the bounded synchronization contract without proving every schedule or unaided learner transfer. Bounded author support only."
    },
